Please note that the performance is normal if the two models are on the save device, or the following lines is committed:
    auto e = cudaHostRegister(ptr, s, cudaHostRegisterDefault);
    if (e != cudaSuccess) {
        spdlog::info("{}", e);
        std::abort();
    }
The following a screenshot of a report from Nsight System, which reveals that before loading the second model on the GPU, there is almost no time gap between the kernel functions:

However, after loading the second model on the GPU, there is a noticeable time gap between the kernel functions:

I kindly request your assistance in investigating this issue and understanding why the performance degradation occurs when cudaHostRegister is used. I believe that resolving this issue would greatly benefit PyTorch users who rely on the JIT module for deployment.
